type": "Bot", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "content_type": "application/x-rpm", "state": "uploaded", "size": 234216897, "digest": "sha256:3e3bdee5f967f5a3eaa2832621d61e321866566e0838e3f76a8ec5b943523245", "download_count": 4, "created_at": "2026-10-21T08:54:31Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-21T08:54:46Z", "browser_download_url": "https://github.com/sandbox-quantum/switch/releases/download/switch-console-v0.40.1/switch-console-x86_64.rpm"}], "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sandbox-quantum/switch/tarball/switch-console-v0.40.1", "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sandbox-quantum/switch/zipball/switch-console-v0.40.1", "body": "## What's Changed\n- Report managed agents and template-made rooms; managed servers point at the current relay (#963)\n- **Fix:** search under agent management shows managed agents, not legacy ones (#975)\n- **Fix:** deleting a managed agent removes the Console agent it was moved from (#974)\n\nPatch backport onto 0.40.0; bundles switch-core 0.31.0.\n\n**Contributors:** @amaudruz \u00b7 @christian-mcdermott\n\n**Full changelog:** https://github.com/sandbox-quantum/switch/compare/switch-console-v0.40.0...switch-console-v0.40.1\n\n---\n\nSwitch Console desktop app 0.40.1 \u2014 macOS Apple silicon + Intel, Linux x64 + arm64, and Windows x64.\n\n**macOS:** download the .dmg for your Mac \u2014 `switch-console-arm64.dmg` for Apple silicon (M1 and later), `switch-console-x64.dmg` for Intel. Not sure which you have? Apple menu \u2192 About This Mac. Open it and drag Switch Console to Applications. Both are signed and notarized with SandboxAQ's Developer ID \u2014 they open without a Gatekeeper bypass, and both receive in-app updates.\n\n**Linux (x64 and arm64):** match your `dpkg --print-architecture`. Download the .AppImage (`chmod +x` then run), the .deb (`sudo apt install ./<file>.deb`) or the .rpm (`sudo dnf install ./<file>.rpm`). Linux builds are unsigned.\n\n**Windows (x64):** run `switch-console-x64.exe`, or use `switch-console-x64.msi` for an `msiexec` install. Both are Authenticode signed as SandboxAQ, so no SmartScreen bypass is needed, and in-app updates verify that signature before installing.", "mentions_count": 2}